# Upload list for `gcloud builds submit` (cloudbuild.yaml).
#
# CRITICAL: without this file, gcloud derives its ignore list from .gitignore, which
# excludes the model weights (engine/data/*.pt, *.npz, qwen_lora/) — the built image
# would then fail at container start. The build-context generator already applies a per-target
# source allowlist, so this global filter should cover only local and secret artifacts.
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
.terraform/
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
engine/data/*.previous
# Build contexts are already created from per-target Git allowlists. Do not globally exclude source
# trees such as docs/, infra/, training/, or spider/: suite/release contexts attest those exact files,
# and the engine context omits them before upload. Ignore only generated/local artifacts below.
.model_taxbak/
scratch/
*.tar.gz
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
# NOTE: tests/ is intentionally NOT ignored — the orchestrator build (cloudbuild.orchestrator.yaml) runs
# tests.test_mcp / tests.test_orchestrator from the upload. It is not copied into the engine image
# (the engine Dockerfile COPYs only engine/), so keeping it costs a tiny upload and nothing in the image.
